Upstream gap: Open WebUI's OpenAI speech settings take only a static key, so
speech-to-text, text-to-speech, and realtime voice calls cannot send the
signed-in user's OAuth token (requested in open-webui#21281; open-webui#21282
was closed unmerged).

Authenticate each of them like the OpenAI connection with the same base URL:
when that connection's auth_type is system_oauth, send the user's OAuth token
instead of the configured key. Text-to-speech covers both the openai and the
openai-realtime engines. Other connection settings, such as custom headers,
still apply to chat only.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release with an auth type for the OpenAI speech
settings.

